"about": "Source table of the catalogue section `thermo`: standard enthalpies of formation at 298.15 K, kJ/mol, of the components of the aqueous network (dissolved species, standard state 1 mol/kg ideal) and of a few other network species whose tabulated value takes precedence over the value derived from the components and the reaction enthalpy of the network (the gases, hydroxide and the hydrogen anions of the key acids). `Hf` absent: unknown (null in the product; the engine then reports heat effects involving the species as not modelled). `from`: the value is derived at build time as Hf(from) minus the formation enthalpy of `from` in the network at 298.15 K, i.e. the tabulated gas value plus the enthalpy of dissolution the network itself uses (entry `derived`). Every other value is typed by hand from the table named by `src` (entry `hand`).",
